# ai-task-manager — local edit backups (do not commit)
.ai-task-manager/templates/*.bak
.ai-task-manager/templates/references/*.bak
# The skill-installed markdown templates + references/ now live under
# .ai-task-manager/templates/ and are tracked in git (#574) — like task-tracker.json
# and the field-config JSONs below — so fresh worktrees and the Test gate receive
# them with no seeding step (#569). Only the `.bak` edit backups stay ignored.
# project-fields.json + project-field-events.json are stable declarative board
# config (schema, aliases, per-transition field-write rules), NOT ephemeral
# caches — tracked in git so fresh worktrees and the Test gate receive them with
# no seeding step (#574). The runtime emit routes through writeIfChanged so a
# refresh of identical content never dirties the tree.
# All machine-local/transient runtime state now lives under .tmp/aitm/ (#573),
# already ignored wholesale via the `.tmp/` rule above: state, queue, fleet,
# cache, orchestrator.lock, locks/, sessions/, gates/, and per-app (app/claude,
# app/codex) trees. No per-file rules needed here.
#
# /.db/ is not SQLite authority (ADR 0002 / #1048). #1217's Assigned → Ready
# for Planning journal still writes
# `<main>/.db/aitm/ready-for-plan-migration.json` from
# ready-for-plan-migration-freeze.mjs if the migrate command is re-applied.
# Ignore the tree so that journal (or a stray empty project.sqlite) cannot
# dirty git status. cf003ad1 removed this rule; restore it.
/.db/
# ai-task-manager — local/runtime artifacts (do not commit)
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

.worktrees/
